{"id": "EUVD-2026-95806", "enisaUuid": "877a9554-db72-30b8-9488-c656da98f5b7", "description": "Xerial snappy-java from 1.1.7.4 before 1.1.10.10 contains a double release vulnerability in SnappyFramedInputStream that returns pooled buffers twice when replacement allocation fails. Attackers can supply framed data with a large declared chunk length to trigger OutOfMemoryError, causing shared backing arrays that expose or overwrite other streams' decompressed data.", "datePublished": "2026-10-09T14:33:28", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T16:04:36", "baseScore": 6.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/xerial/snappy-java/security/advisories/GHSA-c73m-r934-8qvg", "https://github.com/xerial/snappy-java/commit/139a53090a6662298924fd75d21f4769b4a219ea", "https://github.com/xerial/snappy-java/releases/tag/v1.1.10.10", "https://github.com/xerial/snappy-java/blob/v1.1.10.9/src/main/java/org/xerial/snappy/SnappyFramedInputStream.java#L243", "https://github.com/xerial/snappy-java", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/xerial-snappy-java-1.1.7.4-before-1.1.10.10-double-release-of-pooled-buffers-in-snappyframedinputstream"], "aliases": ["GHSA-2xrm-qggp-hr4m", "CVE-2026-108104"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "dd52adfd-e61e-37e0-9d72-8660db970ccb", "product": {"name": "snappy-java", "vendor": {"name": "xerial"}}, "product_version": "1.1.7.4 <1.1.10.10"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "e0109a08-6209-3fa2-9f8b-e6e4fbfb43a0", "vendor": {"name": "xerial"}}], "isExploited": false}